## Personalization Upcharge (Product Page → Cart)

**Option A implemented** (per `docs/collections-architecture.md`): a separate "Monogramming Service" product/variant gets added to the cart alongside the main item, as its own line, when the customer opts into personalization.

### How it works
- `_sections/Product Hero.html` has a section setting **"Monogramming Service Variant ID"** (`li-settings:number`) — merchant enters the numeric variant ID of the Monogramming Service product here, per section instance (i.e. can differ per product if needed, though normally one variant covers all products).
- On click of the Add to Cart button, a small script (separate from and non-interfering with Liquiflow's native `handleVariant` add-to-cart flow) checks whether the personalization checkbox is checked. If so, it fires an independent `POST /cart/add.js` for the configured service variant, carrying the same `properties[...]` (Monogram Style, Text Color, Placement, Monogram Text) as the main item.
- The displayed price next to the checkbox now reads `product.metafields.custom.personalization_cost | money` (per-product, dynamic) instead of a hardcoded "$15".

### Merchant setup required before this works
1. Create a **"Monogramming Service"** product in Shopify Admin, priced at the personalization upcharge.
2. Find its variant ID (Admin → Products → Monogramming Service → variant URL contains the numeric ID, or use the API).
3. In the Theme Editor, open the Product Hero section settings and enter that ID into **"Monogramming Service Variant ID"**.
4. Keep `product.metafields.custom.personalization_cost` in sync with that product's actual price per product — the displayed price and the charged price are two separate places right now (no Shopify Function enforcing they match, per the "no Shopify Plus required" constraint).

If the variant ID setting is left at `0`/unset, the service line item is silently skipped (logged to console) — the main item still adds normally, customer just isn't charged the upcharge. Worth QA-testing before launch.